    "body": "> Currently, I can think of:\r\n\r\nI'm wondering why an app history navigation is treated specifically here, as opposed to a pushState() or replaceState(). The difference between the two is app history navigations have a clear duration, and an additional (async) success or failure signal. But IMO both should be counted as \"navigations\", and that is what https://github.com/WICG/app-history/#performance-timeline-api-integration envisions.",
